# L §5.11 An iteration the law names, copied whole (with taxpayers, iters and the inputs it names).  "init applies
# at i = 0 and beats step"; first(i in iters where c) is the first key whose where is true.  With the steps
# constant (deduction_from_credit and c rows equal at every key), d[t, i] = d0[t] for i ≥ 1 by rule step and at
# i = 0 by rule init, so the first i > 0 with |d[t, i] − d[t, i − 1]| < tolerance is i = 1; deduction = d[t, 1].
# q2: "If no key satisfies the condition within the index, first is refused (RUN-EMPTY)": tolerance 0 makes
# every difference (0) fail "< 0".
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit USD: currency minor 0.01

kind taxpayers
input d0[t in taxpayers]: num USD
input deduction_from_credit[t in taxpayers, i in iters]: num USD
input c[t in taxpayers, i in iters]: num USD
input tolerance: num USD

index iters = 0..50
def d[t in taxpayers, i in iters]: num USD at reader
  rule init beats step = d0[t] when i == 0
  rule step = deduction_from_credit[t, i - 1]

def deduction[t in taxpayers]: num USD = d[t, stop[t]] at reader

def stop[t in taxpayers]: key iters = first(i in iters where i > 0 and abs(d[t, i] - d[t, i - 1]) < tolerance and abs(c[t, i] - c[t, i - 1]) < tolerance) at reader

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  taxpayers + [ann] lives 1980-01-01..
  d0[ann] = 100 USD
  deduction_from_credit[ann, *] = 100 USD
  c[ann, *] = 5 USD
  tolerance = 0.01 USD

version tight
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-06-01
  replace tolerance = 0 USD

ask q1: stop[ann], deduction[ann] law 2026-06-30 as known 2026-05-01
ask q2: stop[ann] law 2026-06-30
=== expect
q1: (1, 100 USD)
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-05-01
q2: refused: RUN-EMPTY ...
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
